codex
The root cause is the audit sandbox’s PID/proc mismatch: child processes report PID 3/4 while `/proc/3` and `/proc/4` do not exist; Lean 4.22 resolves its executable through `/proc/<getpid()>/exe` and therefore aborts. I’ll use a narrowly scoped, recorded `readlink` shim that redirects only `/proc/<pid>/exe` to `/proc/self/exe`, then rerun the same pinned toolchain checks. This affects launcher path discovery, not Lean elaboration or kernel checking.
apply patch
